  "instructions": "Read entries needed for the current task, then follow their $ref dependencies. Common types: ./common-types-basic.json, ./common-types-extended.json and ./common-types-visual.json. Do not load all shards into the model context by default.\nCommon components: ./catalog-components-common.json.\nComposition and repeated layouts: ./catalog-components-composition.json.\nInputs and pickers: ./catalog-components-inputs.json.\nData display and media: ./catalog-components-specialized.json.\nCore functions adapted by DingTalk from A2UI: ./catalog-functions-core.json.\nDingTalk expressions and operators: ./catalog-functions-expressions.json.\nDingTalk host actions: ./catalog-functions-host-actions.json.\nSelect examples from ./examples/README.md; message structures are in ./agent-to-renderer.json.\nThis is the public DingTalk AICard Protocol V0.8 package. Use only the components, fields, functions, and common-type public values listed in the files loaded and assembled for the current scope.\nfallbackMarkdown is an optional DingTalk extension for component-level fallback content. It is used only when the current renderer cannot render the component. Unknown fields and field-validation errors do not trigger it. When omitted, the renderer displays the standard upgrade message.\nSchema references are local file references and require no HTTP access. catalogId is a runtime catalog identifier, not a file path.\nThe #/$defs/anyComponent union describes catalog-specific fields only. Validate complete component instances through the message envelope or loadSchemas().validateComponent, which combines ComponentCommon with this union and rejects unknown fields. The catalog root is not a validation entry point for complete messages or component instances. Complete messages must also conform to the main protocol; dynamic result types, component-tree references, and platform capabilities are validated at runtime.\nExpressions use {\"call\":…, \"args\":…} without an additional profile declaration. A host action must explicitly set functionCall.catalogId to urn:dingtalk:a2ui:host:v1. A public catalog HTTP identifier from a surface or component cannot replace the host Function catalog. For promptText, initialValue is the prefilled-text parameter and text is a result field, not an input parameter.\nAttach form-validation checks to the Button that submits the form. Do not rely on standard event-response fields for automatic write-back.\nUserPicker, ConversationPicker, and ImageUpload require host authorization. Server-side callbacks must still enforce business authorization.",
